  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust owns sidebar pointer/gesture anchors, cumulative deltas, width clamping to 200..480, horizontal RTL reversal, release/capture-loss commit and hide cancellation. Native ResizeArea supplies event delivery, cursor and AX. The existing programmatic delta API remains compatible and uses Rust clamping in Metal mode.",
    "Rust computes main content, sidebar window, edge-reveal target and grip rectangles. The visible sidebar remains at most half the window, with the original 120-point lower cap for very small bounds. A narrow window does not overwrite the stored preferred width.",
    "Rust owns auto-hide guards for pointer leave and deactivation, preserving the original difference in their overlay guards. Native adapters supply pointer containment, pressed-button flags, pin state and open menu/settings/general/tools state. Pin/show/toggle/persistence commands remain native application adapters.",
    "The resize indicator is a Rust display-list primitive on its own two-point-wide Metal surface. It covers only the original inset line rectangle, excluding the existing sidebar canvas, outline and corners. The surface shares the existing GPU device/queue/pipeline and skips identical scenes; no redraw timer or third-party asset was added.",
    "Native grip drawing is gated while its Metal surface is visible. Missing drawables return native fallback painting. Sidebar hide, animation mode and detach hide/release the grip surface through the existing update lifecycle.",
    "The new browser regression physically drags the sidebar 60 points, checks moved page bounds, dispatches a native gesture stream, waits for persistence, narrows/restores the window without overwriting preferred width, exercises auto-hide and edge reveal, preserves the open-settings guard and rejects late drags after hiding.",
    "Prior navigation, split pane, row/folder/pin/tree, scroll, workspace transition, settings, keyboard and large-sidebar regressions remain green."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The matching signed and timestamped final app showed the existing 24-tab demo and Unicode split pair after installing the narrow GPU grip surface; the sidebar outline and rounded corners remained intact.",
    "Switching the sidebar between pinned and overlay modes and hiding/showing it through the header preserved both live pages; the original pinned state was restored before closing the isolated prototype.",
    "The normal application/profile was not used. The prototype launcher exited successfully."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native window/View/ResizeArea containers, event delivery, cursor, focus/AX, pin/show/edge-enter commands, persistence and browser/WebContents commands remain adapters. Edge-indicator painting remains native.",
    "Workspace animation snapshots and remaining palettes/forms/service presentation still require migration.",
    "Physical trackpad, native RTL, VoiceOver, IME and display-scale matrices remain required; Rust RTL arithmetic and native gesture dispatch are narrower evidence.",
    "Controlled real-workload CPU/GPU and actual presentation comparison remains required. Test durations and submitted command buffers do not establish presentation latency or a performance gain.",
    "No new third-party dependency, crate or framework was introduced; original-code Apache-2.0 and required upstream notices are unchanged."
  ]
